    "id": "ncert.maths.ch01.p006.sqrt5_irrational_proof",
    "text": "To prove √5 irrational, suppose √5=a/b in lowest terms with b≠0. Then a²=5b², so the prime-divisibility lemma implies 5 divides a. Write a=5c; substitution gives b²=5c², so 5 divides b too, contradicting coprimality. Thus √5 is irrational.",
