    "id": "ncert.maths.ch13.p007.step_deviation_formula",
    "text": "In the step-deviation method, define uᵢ=(xᵢ−a)/h using an assumed mean a and a non-zero scaling value h. Then x̄ = a + h(Σfᵢuᵢ)/(Σfᵢ). The method is convenient when the deviations share a common factor.",
