    "id": "ncert.maths.ch05.p004.ap_definition",
    "text": "An arithmetic progression (AP) is a list in which the difference between each term and the term immediately before it is constant. This constant difference is the common difference d; for first term a, the terms are a, a+d, a+2d, ….",
